avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1542_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"778"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-12-20T09:01:54-08:00","id":1275529,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1273262#post1273262\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Official character sheets are one of the last things that Onyx Path puts together for a splatbook release. We won't have a Lunar sheet for a while yet.</div> </div> </div> </div>If you think you know what they might need, you can always email the info my way and I'll add it to my to-do list. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://mrgone.rocksolidshells.com/\" target=\"_blank\">MrGone's Character Sheets</a><br /> For all your WoD Character Sheet Needs<br /> _________________________________<br /> Buy books &amp; pdfs from DTRPG and support my web site! <a href=\"http://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse.php?affiliate_id=55414\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a><br /> Support my site on Patreon! <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/mrgone\" target=\"_blank\">Click Here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24-mr-gone","name":"Mr Gone","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24_3.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2695"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T16:50:08-08:00","id":1281721,"title":"","content":"Do we have any more news about upcoming previews, kickstarter dates, or the like?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-19T17:26:56-08:00","id":1281726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1281721#post1281721\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we have any more news about upcoming previews, kickstarter dates, or the like?</div> </div> </div> </div>Because Onyx Path likes to go a month between Kickstarters, it's unlikely there will be another Kickstarter before March. From reading the Monday Meeting Blog, there are a few different things that might have that KS slot, but Lunars does have most of its KS art done already. <br /> <br /> So.... nothing official and no Lunars KS before March at the earliest, possibly much later.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T07:35:38-08:00","id":1281779,"title":"","content":"Thanks! I don't get a lot of forum time lately,. but don't want to miss day one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T09:48:10-08:00","id":1281787,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Simon Darkstep</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1281779#post1281779\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thanks! I don't get a lot of forum time lately,. but don't want to miss day one. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If you check the main Onyx Path site regularly, the Monday Meeting posts will keep you informed about stuff like that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T12:55:14-08:00","id":1281801,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1281726#post1281726\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So.... nothing official and no Lunars KS before March at the earliest, possibly much later.</div> </div> </div> </div>They Came From Beneath the Sea! Kickstarter is ending three days from now. So I think mid to late February isn't impossible, especially if they go Lunars, which they know a lot of people are excited for (okay, maybe I'm also just really hoping it will be soon).<br /> That being said, BrilliantRain is correct that we don't know that Lunars will be the next Kickstarter (going by previous Monday Meeting Notes, it's certainly seems the closest, but that doesn't have to say anything). However, tomorrow there will be another Monday Meeting post and I assume we'll be told the next Kickstarter. I believe they usually also say the starting date. So... we'll know shortly, hopefully.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T13:27:08-08:00","id":1281805,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1281801#post1281801\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> They Came From Beneath the Sea! Kickstarter is ending three days from now. So I think mid to late February isn't impossible, especially if they go Lunars, which they know a lot of people are excited for (okay, maybe I'm also just really hoping it will be soon).<br /> That being said, BrilliantRain is correct that we don't know that Lunars will be the next Kickstarter (going by previous Monday Meeting Notes, it's certainly seems the closest, but that doesn't have to say anything). However, tomorrow there will be another Monday Meeting post and I assume we'll be told the next Kickstarter. I believe they usually also say the starting date. So... we'll know shortly, hopefully.</div> </div> </div> </div>Aberrant is in Manuscript Approval and Hunter 2e is in Development alongside Lunars. Realistically any of those three could get the next KS slot depending on how things go over the next month.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T13:29:51-08:00","id":1281806,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1281805#post1281805\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Aberrant is in Manuscript Approval and Hunter 2e is in Development alongside Lunars. Realistically any of those three could get the next KS slot depending on how things go over the next month.</div> </div> </div> </div>Right. But it's reasonable to assume they will tell us what Kickstarter is next in tomorrow's Monday Meeting Notes, right? So if it isn't Lunars we will know it's going to be late April at the soonest.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T14:03:06-08:00","id":1281814,"title":"","content":"They'd have to pick up a bit on Aberrant, as it's the only one of the three they haven't mentioned doing KS art for yet. That doesn't rule it out, but I wouldn't be surprised if Hunter 2e and Lunars came before it.<br /> <br /> Another candidate is the Scarred Lands Creature Collection 2e, but I'm not quite sure how the KS setup's going to work with that, whether Onyx Path are able to do a KS alongside it because they're letting someone else do this one.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T14:33:00-08:00","id":1281825,"title":"","content":"Thanks for all the replies!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-20T16:35:45-08:00","id":1281840,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wern212</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1281806#post1281806\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Right. But it's reasonable to assume they will tell us what Kickstarter is next in tomorrow's Monday Meeting Notes, right? So if it isn't Lunars we will know it's going to be late April at the soonest.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe. But they might want to give the people more time to work before they announce anything. Plus, both Lunars and Hunter need to be approved by White Wolf, which can take a few weeks and might produce other changes before starting the loop again.<br /> <br /> I\u2019m not saying they definitely won\u2019t announce it tomorrow, but it\u2019s just as likely that they\u2019ll wait until they\u2019re definitely sure they can be ready in time for the KS to announce it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T02:49:15-08:00","id":1281911,"title":"","content":"I'd kind of like them to finish some of the Dragon Blooded and Realm stuff before they start providing Lunars.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T10:16:14-08:00","id":1281965,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1281911#post1281911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd kind of like them to finish some of the Dragon Blooded and Realm stuff before they start providing Lunars.</div> </div> </div> </div>Pushing back preparation for the <i>Lunars</i> Kickstarter wouldn't speed up the release of <i>Dragon-Blooded</i> or <i>The Realm</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted.<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1120-eric-minton","name":"Eric Minton","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1120_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2000"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T11:09:12-08:00","id":1281977,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eric Minton</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1281965#post1281965\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Pushing back preparation for the <i>Lunars</i> Kickstarter wouldn't speed up the release of <i>Dragon-Blooded</i> or <i>The Realm</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>You misunderstand me. Those books could take another three years to come out, and I would still want it to be in a particular order with a certain space of time between them. It's a personal thing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T19:24:50-08:00","id":1282055,"title":"","content":"Hmm, Monday meeting notes says (in Art Notes) KS finals in KS prep begins. I\u2019m not quite sure whether this means Lunars is the next KS or the one after that...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T20:37:24-08:00","id":1282071,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1281977#post1281977\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> You misunderstand me. Those books could take another three years to come out, and I would still want it to be in a particular order with a certain space of time between them. It's a personal thing.</div> </div> </div> </div>I agree, it's not like a production thing, it's more like a hype cycle thing. Right now my brain is mulling all over ideas for DB campaigns and I'm super excited for the Realm to come to us so I can get even more ideas and launch into an awesome campaign for elemental samurai. Or maybe a mortal campaign under the boot heel of imperial oppression. Then after than we can play Lunars and tear it all down. Or build something better. First one then the other, yeah...that one...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-21T20:41:49-08:00","id":1282073,"title":"","content":"I think it does.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Ex3 Craft <a href=\"http://madletter.net/rpg/exalted/maudova/Craft_Rewrite.pdf\" target=\"_blank\">rewrite</a>.<br /> ExEssence <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/18jTwAx0Pldsg5Zt-63HW77zprWvXRTsmz4VrRKZvB8c/edit\" target=\"_blank\">Community Homebrew Compilation</a><br /> Twitter Handle: at maudovajr<br /> Discord Handle: Maudova","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12102-maudova","name":"Maudova","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12102_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T00:00:25-08:00","id":1282093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282055#post1282055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmm, Monday meeting notes says (in Art Notes) KS finals in KS prep begins. I\u2019m not quite sure whether this means Lunars is the next KS or the one after that...</div> </div> </div> </div>Based on prior history, it means Lunars are next - they've got the final KS art in, and are now preparing the Kickstarter. Should be sometime in the next few weeks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T00:21:46-08:00","id":1282094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282071#post1282071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, it's not like a production thing, it's more like a hype cycle thing. Right now my brain is mulling all over ideas for DB campaigns and I'm super excited for the Realm to come to us so I can get even more ideas and launch into an awesome campaign for elemental samurai. Or maybe a mortal campaign under the boot heel of imperial oppression. Then after than we can play Lunars and tear it all down. Or build something better. First one then the other, yeah...that one...</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough if that's the case, but my brain has been in the hype cycle for lunars since the core dropped. So I can't wait. I was somewhat surprised to see no new Kickstarter announced with the newest MMN.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T02:58:21-08:00","id":1282103,"title":"","content":"Personally, while extra DB stuff is nice, basic Lunars stuff would simply be more useful. I can run a DB game now, I can't run a Lunars game.<br /> So I'd rather have Lunars first, then the extra DB stuff, then Exigents, then the extra Lunar stuff, etc.<br /> <br /> Honestly, I got the DB KS text nearly a year ago. The hype cycle on DB has wound down for me.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I assumed they'd want to get the Lunars KS released by March at the latest, because I think they'll want to be able to say that the Lunars KS was released within a year of the DB KS. And that looks like it'll happen. Which is great!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T03:38:59-08:00","id":1282107,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282103#post1282103\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Honestly, I got the DB KS text nearly a year ago. The hype cycle on DB has wound down for me.</div> </div> </div> </div>This makes me think of a weird kind of layering in Exalted consumers. If you took part in the Kickstarter, you've had Dragon Blooded for about a year, and are ready for Lunars. If you didn't, you're still waiting on that release by the time all of the hype and attention shifts to Lunars, and have only had little releases of enemies to tide you over in the meantime. It feels a bit fragmentary.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T03:55:14-08:00","id":1282109,"title":"","content":"Oh yeah. It seems really weird to me that the Dragonblood book still isn't technically out, when my friends have been playing a 3rd ed Dragonblood game for a year, I play a mixed game with a Dragonblood member, and I've been considering whether to play a DB after this arc ends and I retire my Solar for, what, about 8 months?<br /> <br /> I got a lift from an old friend the other day, whose gaming group had recently tried Exalted 3rd ed, and the players liked it but the ST got frustrated with just having the Core antagonists, which didn't at all challenge four combat-orientated Solars, and gave up. I guess he couldn't go to Drivethru and see the Dragonblood book, because it's not actually out. And while I like the monthly releases (because, frankly, I buy the ones I like the look of and not the boring ones or ones similar to something I could easily make myself), someone who doesn't pay attention to Exalted so much would probably miss them.<br /> (Once they're in a proper book, that'll probably be easier, as people will go &quot;oh, that's the Monster Manual, I should get that to run the game.)<br /> <br /> <br /> I mean, I'm not sure there's any good alternative (unless you could go back in time to when funding models for rpgs were different). But it still does maybe feel a bit weird.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-22-2019, 07:01 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T04:35:06-08:00","id":1282111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282109#post1282109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mean, I'm not sure there's any good alternative (unless you could go back in time to when funding models for rpgs were different).</div> </div> </div> </div>I want to analyse this line a bit, but first I'd want to be sure exactly what you mean by it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T05:09:40-08:00","id":1282115,"title":"","content":"Well, basically most RPGs, other than DnD (ie the one with the most money), get Kickstarted now. I assume this is because of economic and advertising reasons.<br /> <br /> When they do Kickstarters, I think they do far better when they promise to release the text as part of the KS. I assume that's why OP does that with most of their KSs now. People back because they want the text, but also people know that the text is done, so they're not going to have to wait years (my friend who invested like \u00a3100 in the Exalted Core KS was very annoyed that he had to wait years to get anything, but was mollified with Dragonblood because he knew the text was written and he'd get it straight away). I myself didn't back the Core, but backed the Dragonblood Kickstarter. And while I'm still waiting for my copy of Heirs and the Realm (I think that was on the backer tier? I don't remember), I got the text of Dragonblood pretty much straight away, so I'm happy, and will back Lunars.<br /> <br /> But, if they a)do Kickstarters, and b)release the text as part of that Kickstarter, then you're going to get this disconnect in the development cycle between backers and non-backers (and, frankly, that's a tool to get people to back; a kind of early-access pass).<br /> <br /> Saying that, I believe it's possible to get the stuff already released on the Kickstart page by backing now, even though the KS finished? I think maybe someone said that? Not sure.<br /> But it's easy to miss if you didn't know about it.<br /> <br /> So, maybe there's some way to make that better known? Advertising, links on the Onyx Path shop? Something on Drivethru would be most useful.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T05:29:03-08:00","id":1282121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282115#post1282115\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, basically most RPGs, other than DnD (ie the one with the most money), get Kickstarted now. I assume this is because of economic and advertising reasons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Onyx Path, at least, maintains that publication isn't dependant on Kickstarter success, and the funding is for the high quality prestige printings. I see no reason to dispute that assertion.<br /> <br /> The commensurate increase in making those printings, well... I want to say it's somewhere between taking advantage of an opportunity and a perceived need to maintain the esteem of the brand.<br /> <br /> Still, there are a few reasons that I'd like some more books that would have been soft covers in the past. Primarily just for the content they would entail.<br /> <br /> If you have me the choice between kickstarting Lunars and regular publishing two or three sixty page setting books, I'd actually want the latter first, just from a sense that almost nothing but Exalted hardbacks both makes the whole thing feel a bit too heavy to me, and kind of does make it feel like attention can't be spared for that setting development.<br /> <br /> I think there's a lot good in Adversaries and Hundred Devils, but think some of them are missing a bit of context.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T06:06:19-08:00","id":1282127,"title":"","content":"It helps that now the funding also goes towards producing a second book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T07:17:44-08:00","id":1282132,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282071#post1282071\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I agree, it's not like a production thing, it's more like a hype cycle thing. Right now my brain is mulling all over ideas for DB campaigns and I'm super excited for the Realm to come to us so I can get even more ideas and launch into an awesome campaign for elemental samurai. Or maybe a mortal campaign under the boot heel of imperial oppression. Then after than we can play Lunars and tear it all down. Or build something better. First one then the other, yeah...that one...</div> </div> </div> </div>Kind of like how we got a few years with nothing but Solars to play with?<br /> <br /> But at least with Lunars coming out sooner after Dragon-Blooded than Dragon-Blooded after Lunars, storytellers will have a better idea of the Silver Anathema that their players are more likely to confront.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T10:31:13-08:00","id":1282151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282093#post1282093\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Based on prior history, it means Lunars are next - they've got the final KS art in, and are now preparing the Kickstarter. Should be sometime in the next few weeks.</div> </div> </div> </div>Keep in mind that the Lunars manuscript is still in Development and needs to go through approval before the KS and that can take a month and might produce problems that need addressing which can take additional time. I doubt OP is going to push back a KS by more than a week or two, so they might just put another project in place and juggle the schedule a bit. And there are three other things that could get KSs at about the same level as Lunars, so....<br /> <br /> It really all depends on what gets done first.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T10:43:49-08:00","id":1282153,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282121#post1282121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Onyx Path, at least, maintains that publication isn't dependant on Kickstarter success, and the funding is for the high quality prestige printings. I see no reason to dispute that assertion.<br /> <br /> The commensurate increase in making those printings, well... I want to say it's somewhere between taking advantage of an opportunity and a perceived need to maintain the esteem of the brand.<br /> <br /> Still, there are a few reasons that I'd like some more books that would have been soft covers in the past. Primarily just for the content they would entail.<br /> <br /> If you have me the choice between kickstarting Lunars and regular publishing two or three sixty page setting books, I'd actually want the latter first, just from a sense that almost nothing but Exalted hardbacks both makes the whole thing feel a bit too heavy to me, and kind of does make it feel like attention can't be spared for that setting development.<br /> <br /> I think there's a lot good in Adversaries and Hundred Devils, but think some of them are missing a bit of context.</div> </div> </div> </div>As far as it goes, The Realm is in layout and is getting art as we speak. So that\u2019s probably a few months, but it should be out this year. And Across the Eight Directions is being actively worked on alongside Lunars, so maybe next year for that one. By then we might have a compiled Hundred Devils book too.<br /> <br /> So, they are working on the setting stuff and it is coming and the gameline will probably feel much more substantial in 2020. Which doesn\u2019t exactly help right now, I get it, but short of finding some way to get a text only version of The Realm, there\u2019s really not much they can do but keep working.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T11:17:11-08:00","id":1282160,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282153#post1282153\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, they are working on the setting stuff and it is coming and the gameline will probably feel much more substantial in 2020.</div> </div> </div> </div>One <i>more</i> reason to look forward to 2020.<br /> <br /> Can anyone lend me a time machine?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T12:57:33-08:00","id":1282184,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282160#post1282160\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One <i>more</i> reason to look forward to 2020.<br /> <br /> Can anyone lend me a time machine?</div> </div> </div> </div>And miss one of America's two major political parties dying a messy death in real time? Possibly even both of them?<br /> <br /> Fine, but I'll be taking your share of the popcorn.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T13:14:30-08:00","id":1282190,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282132#post1282132\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kind of like how we got a few years with nothing but Solars to play with?<br /> <br /> But at least with Lunars coming out sooner after Dragon-Blooded than Dragon-Blooded after Lunars, storytellers will have a better idea of the Silver Anathema that their players are more likely to confront.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeaaah hopefully not quite so long as the exclusively Solar run. Although it did give me a chance to run/play in 4 campaigns with Solars only and let me do a lot of what you can only really do with Solars, so it wasn't so bad.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T14:45:34-08:00","id":1282199,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282107#post1282107\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This makes me think of a weird kind of layering in Exalted consumers. If you took part in the Kickstarter, you've had Dragon Blooded for about a year, and are ready for Lunars. If you didn't, you're still waiting on that release by the time all of the hype and attention shifts to Lunars, and have only had little releases of enemies to tide you over in the meantime. It feels a bit fragmentary.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is what I'm dealing with. I'm so far behind everyone else now as far as knowing anything about the game I may have to give up on it","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T14:59:24-08:00","id":1282202,"title":"","content":"Isn't there a way to get the DB book on the KS page? I'm sure someone said that.<br /> If not, well, I think it should be out in a few months at most.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-22T17:22:55-08:00","id":1282222,"title":"","content":"Yep, you can preorder here: <a href=\"https://what-fire-has-wrought.backerkit.com/hosted_preorders\" target=\"_blank\">https://what-fire-has-wrought.backer...sted_preorders</a><br /> <br /> Gives you the pdf when you do.<br /> <br /> The Kickstarter hype is there to draw attention to the game and get the word out. While also allowing for expanding of wordcount and supplements. Just by kickstarting 5 dollars you get access to the manuscript. Onyx Path then puts the product up on backerkit when the Kickstarter is finished so people can preorder and grab the books after its over. Outside of monetary issues there's no reason anyone can't get caught up.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":717,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","user":"Monghani","date":". 01-22-2019, 08:27 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T22:38:04-08:00","id":1282388,"title":"","content":"So, the <a href=\"https://www.kickstarter.com/projects/200664283/dragon-blooded-what-fire-has-wrought-for-exalted-3/posts/2394881\" target=\"_blank\">new update for the Dragon-Blooded Kickstarter</a> is suggesting rather subtly that Lunars will be the next Kickstarter, and comments on the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/they-came-from-the-last-few-days-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">Monday Meeting Notes</a> made by RichT seem to indicate the same.<br /> <br /> My body is ready, my wallet isn't.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-23T23:51:06-08:00","id":1282395,"title":"","content":"i guess I should get in on this one","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T06:51:06-08:00","id":1282424,"title":"","content":"A threshold question for me: does Lunars still use the stunt-based excellency structure from the core book? (Of course, I understand if that's not allowed to be answered at this point.<br /> <br /> I <i>really</i> want to recreate my 2E lunar martial artist, literally my favorite RPG character ever, but that excellency loses me for the lunar kickstarter and likely the book itself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T07:11:16-08:00","id":1282426,"title":"","content":"Obviously we haven't seen the book yet, but I'm 90% sure it will do. Eska of the Seven Blades, the Lunar character in Antagonists of the Righteous (whom I guess is partly there to preview Lunars) still uses the same stunt-based excellency. She also can raise her soak by her Stamina/2, or (Stamina+appropriate Attribute)/2 with a stunt.<br /> <br /> Personally, I dislike it too (though not as much as you, by the sound of it; it's an annoyance but wouldn't put me off Lunars), but it seems quite popular generally. I have a feeling there was a mention that it was popular with playtesters. So I'd be (pleasantly) surprised if it doesn't make it into the book.<br /> <br /> (I can understand why it's popular. We used to love stunts back in the day. Not anymore though.)<br /> <br /> I hope to run a Lunars game in future (probably next year I guess, as our group has 3 games that I think will finish late this year), so I may houserule it or something. Not sure.<br /> <br /> What my players did with Lunar PCs (we have a few) is just picking an attribute they think that makes sense, and using that for the cap without telling me. Which arguably is a bit dodgy, but it certainly saved time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T10:09:34-08:00","id":1282449,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282424#post1282424\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A threshold question for me: does Lunars still use the stunt-based excellency structure from the core book? (Of course, I understand if that's not allowed to be answered at this point.<br /> <br /> I <i>really</i> want to recreate my 2E lunar martial artist, literally my favorite RPG character ever, but that excellency loses me for the lunar kickstarter and likely the book itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, one, what do you think about the possibility of Lunars being able to combine Martial Arts Charms with their own combat-based Attribute Charms?<br /> <br /> Two, whhhhhyyyyyyy?!?!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T10:26:21-08:00","id":1282452,"title":"","content":"Lunar Martial Artists in DBT are going to be sweeet.<br /> <br /> I'm not exactly sure how good yet, because I don't know if there will be a damage cap, but even without that I can counterattack with Snake Style using a Lunar charm (Coiled Serpent Defence), I can combine Snake poisons and Adder Fang Method (and if there are any other blanket poison-boosting charms, I may be able to use them with Snake Style poisons), etc.<br /> <br /> Mostly, it's just more convenient. You don't have to worry about which charms can or can't work together like with Solars.<br /> <br /> If there isn't a damage cap... ooh... comboing Snake's soak with all the Lunar soak charms. Comboing the Strength excellency, Striking Cobra Technique, DBT, some more Lunar strength charms and then Armour-Penetrating Fang Strike... expensive, but brutal.<br /> <br /> I haven't got into a fight yet (only played for 3 sessions) with my Lunar, but it's going to be fun.<br /> <br /> Saying all this, obviously the downside is that MA are useless in animal shapes, but most &quot;Lunar Martial Artist&quot; concepts I've seen do indeed fight in human/DBT form, and aren't fussed about combat shapechanging, so that's fine.<br /> (I don't have any combat forms really. Unless you count a snake for slithering up and biting people, or a horse. But my old Lunar had a Bear and Tyrant Lizard, and those are no good for MA.)<br /> <br /> (With the excelleny... I guess if we hate it we can just not worry about it too much. It's an option after all, not something necessary, and it does cost motes. Just break it out when it's really important, as we tend to do with stunts generally. But since my players were doing it without stunting, I doubt my ST will mind much if I don't.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-24-2019, 01:42 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T10:42:20-08:00","id":1282456,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282449#post1282449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, one, what do you think about the possibility of Lunars being able to combine Martial Arts Charms with their own combat-based Attribute Charms?</div> </div> </div> </div> THE NEW HOTNESS!<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282449#post1282449\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Two, whhhhhyyyyyyy?!?!</div> </div> </div> </div> The short answer is that I don't find it to be fun in the least, which is problematic for magic that is used so often. A longer answer is beyond the scope of this thread (and I'm skeptical of the value of challenging orthodox positions on this forum).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T11:09:20-08:00","id":1282463,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282456#post1282456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The short answer is that I don't find it to be fun in the least, which is problematic for magic that is used so often. A longer answer is beyond the scope of this thread (and I'm skeptical of the value of challenging orthodox positions on this forum).</div> </div> </div> </div>For what it's worth while I like the general shape of the excellency, I have serious concerns about the playability. I'm withholding judgement until I see the final text, but I'm worried about relying on a very fuzzy gm call for it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8977-sigfriedmcwild","name":"sigfriedmcwild","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8977_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T11:53:11-08:00","id":1282474,"title":"","content":"Hmmm.... I can understand the dilemma. If you leave Lunars with the base cap of Attribute, their excellency is worse than that of a DB. If you make it Attribute *2 or something, then it\u2019s as good or better than Solars. Even just going Attribute+Essence (which would probably work fine for most games) runs into the twin problems of 1) you want Lunars to be a bit more restricted than Solars and 2) Lunars probably have the largest number of active and powerful elders out there, so there\u2019s actually a bunch who would be able to max out an att+essence cap.<br /> <br /> So, the current one is a nice way to thread the needle, by restricting a Lunar to the base cap most of the time, but letting them reach beyond once in a while. The two problems I see it running into are 1) if people start feeling like the cap should be two Attributes all the time, they\u2019ll feel like they\u2019re losing something whenever they can\u2019t get the higher cap and 2) the circumstances of when you get the higher cap are fuzzy and can\u2019t always be predicted, so you might be stuck in a situation where you need more dice, make what you feel is a legitimate stunt, and the ST says No and then problems start.<br /> <br /> Personally, I think it works, but I think other stuff could work too. Whenever the KS gets to the charms chapter, it might be worth starting a dedicated thread to discuss the Excellency. Even if they devs won\u2019t decide on a new cap at that date, they might be willing to add more discussion of the cap to the book if enough people think it\u2019s warranted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T12:00:51-08:00","id":1282476,"title":"","content":"I will also note that, most of the time when I\u2019m adding dice to a roll, I only add 4, because that keeps my anima from flaring. I only go for the full amount when I\u2019m really under pressure or when I\u2019m doing a downtime thing and Essence isn\u2019t as big a deal. That doesn\u2019t necessarily prevent the ST and I from disagreeing about whether my stunt is legit or not, but it does mean I\u2019m not going to need to stunt every single roll, just the really important ones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T12:24:47-08:00","id":1282480,"title":"","content":"Other potential things I could see some players having problems with, although not me specifically.<br /> <br /> People who feel like they must max out their stuff with 5s now need their ability and at least two attributes at 5, but best be 3 to be safe. Much easier to come up with stunts combining alternating abilities since stunts fail automatically if they\u2019re boring and repetitive. Although Lunars are attributes exalted so...<br /> <br /> Some attributes, notably strength and intelligence, lend themselves really really well to being mixed into other stuff. Basically any physical task ever could benefit from enhanced strength, even dexterous ones like wielding a fencing foil or tightrope walking. Similarly almost any mental or social task, and even physical ones even, can easily be stunted with \u201cI\u2019m so smart I figure out X helpful strategy to lift this/convince this/spot this thing\u201d. Some people might find that kind of imbalance distasteful. <br /> <br /> Then again the martial arts combining thing is so cool, like, why bother getting upset over it. Tiger man using Tiger Style will just be able to tear a horde of fair folk cataphracts apart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T12:33:42-08:00","id":1282481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282456#post1282456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> THE NEW HOTNESS!<br /> <br /> The short answer is that I don't find it to be fun in the least, which is problematic for magic that is used so often. A longer answer is beyond the scope of this thread (and I'm skeptical of the value of challenging orthodox positions on this forum).</div> </div> </div> </div>It ought to be fun, thinking of how to combine different stuff. But, in my opinion, in practice it generally won't be for our play group.* Hopefully it will be for others.<br /> And there are other reasons. But I think I've said them on this forum before.<br /> <br /> *I say from the experience of having played with 1-2 Lunar PCs in 2 different games for about 2 years (or 3? When did the Core come out?). Most of their charms were custom, from Irked's rules, or whatever, but the excellency we used as-is since it's from the Core.<br /> In those three years, I could count the amount of times I heard a Lunar player in either game do a stunt and ask to use a second attribute on the fingers of one hand.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">So, the current one is a nice way to thread the needle, by restricting a Lunar to the base cap most of the time, but letting them reach beyond once in a while.</div> </div> </div> </div>But haven't I heard many times on this forum that you should stunt every single action?<br /> <br /> I mean, you certainly can stunt most stuff.<br /> <br /> I like the idea that a Lunar has a low cap most of the time but when it counts can break out a bigger cap. But I think there's better ways to do it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-24-2019, 03:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T13:39:45-08:00","id":1282500,"title":"","content":"With respect, I didn't mean to start a discussion about the merit of the Lunar excellency as presented in the core book, as that seems outside the scope of the thread; I just wanted to post the question to the OP.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/415-equitable-remedy","name":"Equitable Remedy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar415_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"114"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T13:49:18-08:00","id":1282505,"title":"","content":"No worries, we'll move on then.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T16:41:06-08:00","id":1282542,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Equitable Remedy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282456#post1282456\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm skeptical of the value of challenging orthodox positions on this forum).</div> </div> </div> </div>I completely get that, because if I'm being 100% honest, at the time I posted that question I was gearing myself up for a... maybe not a fight, but at least a contentious (and maybe a bit acidic) response.<br /> <br /> With the benefit of a few hours (and a suitably abashing pre-empt on your part), I've cooled down a lot, so I wouldn't pursue that. I'd hope for more dialogue for the sake of including lots of viewpoints rather than trying to convince one another of stuff, but... I get it, I get how hostile the place can feel at times and not wanting to deal with wading into it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T20:34:01-08:00","id":1282571,"title":"","content":"I still do think we should open a thread specifically to discuss the excellency once that section of the Lunars manuscript becomes available.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T21:29:05-08:00","id":1282578,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>BrilliantRain</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282571#post1282571\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still do think we should open a thread specifically to discuss the excellency once that section of the Lunars manuscript becomes available.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m trying to figure out why folk don\u2019t like it? <br /> <br /> 1. It\u2019s optional to stunt and due to flaring you won\u2019t see it all the time.<br /> <br /> 2. It\u2019s using a mechanic you would have used for the roll anyway (Stunting, just work it in as part of the description for the +2 d10 and the extra stat on excellency) Gives Lunars their own stunting bonus, really.<br /> <br /> 3. It\u2019s easy to ignore if you want to (ST just says you always bring in the other highest stat for max Excellency Calculation)<br /> <br /> And for those of us who want to Model Robert Downey Jr\u2019s Sherlock 10 moves ahead Bartitsu, excellent stunt fodder. \ud83d\ude06","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-24T21:54:41-08:00","id":1282583,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282121#post1282121\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Onyx Path, at least, maintains that publication isn't dependant on Kickstarter success, and the funding is for the high quality prestige printings. I see no reason to dispute that assertion.<br /> <br /> The commensurate increase in making those printings, well... I want to say it's somewhere between taking advantage of an opportunity and a perceived need to maintain the esteem of the brand.</div> </div> </div> </div> I believe that it's not just the better printing quality, but also the money to get better stuff in it; without kickstarter they'd have basic books with all the minimal stuff, but the extra fiction, some extra illustrations, area descriptions and kicking in extra thin books sometimes.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T03:26:44-08:00","id":1282610,"title":"","content":"anyone remember, back on a previous forum, the thread someone made to show the difference between a warform and a furry?<br /> <br /> <br /> I'm trying to remember how that went. I just remember it was kinda funny.<br /> <br /> I am hoping we don't need it here though","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1047-vampire-hunter-d","name":"vampire hunter D","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1047_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1727"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T07:25:49-08:00","id":1282633,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282578#post1282578\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I\u2019m trying to figure out why folk don\u2019t like it?<br /> <br /> 1. It\u2019s optional to stunt and due to flaring you won\u2019t see it all the time.<br /> <br /> 2. It\u2019s using a mechanic you would have used for the roll anyway (Stunting, just work it in as part of the description for the +2 d10 and the extra stat on excellency) Gives Lunars their own stunting bonus, really.<br /> <br /> 3. It\u2019s easy to ignore if you want to (ST just says you always bring in the other highest stat for max Excellency Calculation)<br /> <br /> And for those of us who want to Model Robert Downey Jr\u2019s Sherlock 10 moves ahead Bartitsu, excellent stunt fodder. \ud83d\ude06</div> </div> </div> </div>Can only speak personally but the concerns that I saw are as follows.<br /> <br /> 1. Not using limits you to only five dice max, (more likely 3 or 4 given how attribute dots are rarer than ability dots) Which feels pretty weak.<br /> <br /> 2. The strength of the stunting mechanic was how broad of a umbrella it cast, this is lost with the excellency because you can't just stunt you have to stunt with a particular attribute. You are not just stunting once either. If you are fighting anything tougher than a bear you a going to need all the dice you can get which means stunting every attack and defence and coming up with new way to justify how your charisma helps you punch.<br /> <br /> 3. well yea, if a player in my group ever wanted to play a lunar I would just let them add a second attribute for free no stunt required, still kind of annoying to do though.<br /> <br /> Though I suppose it is a bit of a moot point right now. With the kickstarter right around the corner we should have a more clear picture soon.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T08:22:41-08:00","id":1282644,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282633#post1282633\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">1. Not using limits you to only five dice max, (more likely 3 or 4 given how attribute dots are rarer than ability dots) Which feels pretty weak.</div> </div> </div> </div>Considering that's how Lunar die adders always worked, they're no worse off than they ever were.<br /> <br /> Considering how previously, their means of increasing the die cap added Essence to the equation, and required a short-lived Charm to go into a berserker rage, they're actually a bit better off than they were before.<br /> <br /> It's an Excellency that can affect things that Ability Excellencies simply can't, like soak and damage, and it takes far fewer purchases to get a full set that can be added to any possible roll.<br /> <br /> How strong should it be?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. The strength of the stunting mechanic was how broad of a umbrella it cast, this is lost with the excellency because you can't just stunt you have to stunt with a particular attribute.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can still do regular stunts? What, should the upgrade be unlimited?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you are fighting anything tougher than a bear you a going to need all the dice you can get which means stunting every attack and defence</div> </div> </div> </div>That sounds like it will burn out your mote pool fairly quickly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">coming up with new way to justify how your charisma helps you punch.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or any of seven other Attributes.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">well yea, if a player in my group ever wanted to play a lunar I would just let them add a second attribute for free no stunt required, still kind of annoying to do though.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, you do think it should be unlimited. To have a dice cap equivalent to that of Solars. For a much smaller and more broadly applicable range of stats.<br /> <br /> Seems a bit overpowered.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T08:30:35-08:00","id":1282648,"title":"","content":"Shall I just start another thread about the excellency specifically? Because otherwise it probably will **** all over this thread.<br /> <br /> Or should we just accept that and make this the Lunar excellency thread?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T08:34:33-08:00","id":1282649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282648#post1282648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Shall I just start another thread about the excellency specifically? Because otherwise it probably will **** all over this thread.</div> </div> </div> </div>What is this thread about at the moment?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T08:36:33-08:00","id":1282650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282649#post1282649\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> What is this thread about at the moment?</div> </div> </div> </div>I was about to ask the same thing. The original post was &quot;I was in the playtest and it was awesome.&quot; We're nowhere near that now. Lunar-thread gonna Lunar, but yeah I'm not sure what point this thread is supposed to be serving at the moment to even get derailed <i>from</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T08:38:09-08:00","id":1282652,"title":"","content":"Well it was about when Lunars was coming out, and how awesome it'll be.<br /> <br /> If you come to the forum wondering when Lunars is out, and read a thread with people complaining about the excellency, it might put you off. (I'm very excited about Lunars. I don't like the excellency, or at least how it looks now, but it's the only thing so far I dislike. And I know others will like it.)<br /> <br /> I don't mind carrying on, but Equitable Remedy didn't really want to turn this thread into the &quot;What do you think about the Lunar excellency thread&quot; when they asked about it, and I'm trying to respect that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-25-2019, 11:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T08:47:50-08:00","id":1282654,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282652#post1282652\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well it was about when Lunars was coming out, and how awesome it'll be.</div> </div> </div> </div>A topic that lasted for about a page and a half over three days before dropping off for close to two months prior to somebody used it for generic Kickstarter enquiries.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">If you come to the forum wondering when Lunars is out, and read a thread with people complaining about the excellency, it might put you off.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well first, I'm not sure that's much of an expectation to carry to a thread with such a non-descript title.<br /> <br /> Second, this sounds like an argument against having any contentious discussion about Lunars at all.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T10:51:09-08:00","id":1282677,"title":"","content":"If it's predictable that a stunt-based dice cap it will cause a problem for your group, isn't it pretty easy to simply adopt a different dice cap for your group and move on? &quot;150% of Attribute&quot;, or &quot;Attribute +3&quot;, or &quot;Attribute + Essence&quot;, or &quot;Attribute + Ability&quot;?<br /> <br /> I grant a preference for something you don't have to Rule Zero is valid. And having to Rule Zero something can be disruptive if the group has conflict over the necessity. But dice caps sure seem like one of the easiest Rule Zeros, unless I'm missing something.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T10:56:28-08:00","id":1282678,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282677#post1282677\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But dice caps sure seem like one of the easiest Rule Zeros, unless I'm missing something.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd say there's a question about what an altered dice cap does to the overall power of a type, whether it ends up making the Excellency patently superior to other Charms, and how much a mote pool can support it.<br /> <br /> Plus the matter of balancing the broader applicability of Attributes.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T11:11:25-08:00","id":1282684,"title":"","content":"Yeah, it's hard to balance.<br /> <br /> Also, house-ruling is actually, in practice, a bit of a hassle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-25-2019, 02:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T14:50:21-08:00","id":1282725,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282644#post1282644\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>1. Never played 1st or 2nd Edition, were lunars fun and interesting in them? If so that makes me feel a lot better about the dice cap, I have only been comparing them to Third edition solars and DB's.<br /> 2. As for overpowered maybe? A lunar needs to spend twice as many attribute dots and twice as many bonus points to match a solar in a single ability and I have no idea if that is fair without seeing the rest of the charms","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T14:50:58-08:00","id":1282726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282678#post1282678\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd say there's a question about what an altered dice cap does to the overall power of a type, whether it ends up making the Excellency patently superior to other Charms, and how much a mote pool can support it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Obviously it requires a <i>bit</i> of thought, but how much more than asking, &quot;How often did the devs expect the cap to be stunted up, and how much does that usually raise the cap?&quot; I mean, if the answer is, &quot;Pretty much whenever it's actually important, and by 4&quot;, a flat Attribute +4 is going to be pretty close to balanced, and miscalculation that leaves it at +3 or +5 isn't going to be that big of a deal. Heck, if Lunars itself doesn't have a sidebar of Storyteller guidance about how much/how often it's expected players will succeed at stunting up the cap, that's arguably a defect in the book we should yell about no matter how you feel about the mechanic.<br /> <br /> I guess I'm mentally comparing this to 3e complaints like &quot;I don't like the Craft system&quot; or &quot;I don't like withering combat&quot; or &quot;ugh, Wyld Shaping is messy&quot; or &quot;I need more mechanical bureaucracy system help!&quot; Getting stuck with a die-cap-increasing mechanism you don't like is a valid complaint, but strikes me as far more manageable at the table. And it certainly isn't 2e lethality/perfects . . .","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T17:23:54-08:00","id":1282747,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282725#post1282725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Never played 1st or 2nd Edition, were lunars fun and interesting in them? If so that makes me feel a lot better about the dice cap, I have only been comparing them to Third edition solars and DB's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Wow, that's a heck of a question. Short answer, yes they certainly had fun and interesting things in them. How much of 3rd editions DBs have you played with so far, if you don't mind me asking? Because the Lunar excellencies have very nearly the DB's cap, always. In fact barring the specialty bump it's equal. It's also way way more broadly applicable.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282725#post1282725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">2. As for overpowered maybe? A lunar needs to spend twice as many attribute dots and twice as many bonus points to match a solar in a single ability and I have no idea if that is fair without seeing the rest of the charms</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, attribute exalted have always been kind of unique in that regard because of broad applications of them. Consider this instead:<br /> <br /> A super physical Lunar who's got high strength and dex and stamina, but picks up a charisma excellency with like 2 in the stat, so any time she rolls on a charisma skill she can add up to 7 dice as long as she stunts in her impressive muscles or graceful movement. So even with zero dots in socialize, presence, performance, or war she can get 11 dice as a base roll, including the stunt. That's a pretty big power cap for the investment of a single charm. It's true that you won't be able to stunt in physical stats for all of those rolls, but for any time you want to use war to command, or performance to dance, or presence to intimidate or <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=XJ-WohANo00&amp;feature=youtu.be&amp;t=35\" target=\"_blank\">inspire</a>, you can pretty easily stunt it when you need it. You can also show off and flaunt your grace with socialize/presence/performance using dexterity to entrance your target, it's going to be ST dependent, but it shouldn't be too hard, especially if you're not doing it constantly.<br /> <br /> The Solar mirror of that is somebody who has 1 charisma and a small handful of ability dots spread out among those abilities. To even catch up to the Lunar's 9 (before stunt) dice in those abilities, the Solar needs to put all of her social stats to the minimum requirements of their first charm, buy all of their first charms, and then bump her charisma up to 2-3. Admittedly they now have a utility charm in each of those trees, but they're also 3 charms, 2 attribute dots and a smattering of ability dots behind.<br /> <br /> In that case you're not matching the Solar for raw power, but that's a losing battle anyway, you're never going to beat a Solar at being good at anything. You can, however, with a single charm purchase take yourself from &quot;No mortal writeup in the corebook has as bad a (Charisma + Presence) roll as I do&quot; to &quot;I have a better (Charisma + {various}) roll than the glittering, bejeweled earth elemental diplomat in the corebook.&quot; So that's at least different from what a Solar can do in a unique way.<br /> <br /> <br /> EDIT: Actually, that's part of the key to enjoying any non-Solar thing in Exalted. Never think &quot;Yeah, but a Solar can...&quot; because they probably can do whatever you can better, easier, cheaper. Instead look at the things that your character's splat does differently, like shapeshifting or broad excellencies. Or in the case of a DB a chargen Crane Stylist gets access to the first 7 charms, where as any non-MA-supernal gets access to 2, that's kind of cool.<br /> <br /> If the raw power is really what you want though, you should probably just think about playing really cool Solar concepts, they're just dandy in most cases.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1121,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","user":"DrLoveMonkey","date":". 01-25-2019, 08:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T18:02:31-08:00","id":1282755,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282747#post1282747\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">snip</div> </div> </div> </div>For DB I played about 20ish sessions I think? Across a couple of groups. I like them but (without getting too much of a tangent) their charmset is the thing that least pulled in my groups. It was their fluff and place in the world as princes of the earth that really sold them.<br /> <br /> As for the excellency I agree it can be very powerful. I should apologize though my first post on the matter was unclear and I should of waited longer after getting out of bed. My main observation was less that the excellency was objectively weak and more that it could subjectively feel weak to a new player.<br /> <br /> So how do you deal with a player who likes lunars but is bad at stunting very specific things like attributes? A lot of the players I know only stunt as much as they do because of how easy it is to work in a scene. If I told them they had to stunt in a attribute it would happen a lot less.<br /> <br /> Also since I see I failed to make it clear in previous posts I do not think the excellency should be changed primarily because I do not know what a good replacement for it would be. My point on letting my group just combine attributes to get a higher cap was mostly tailored to the fact I know they are not going to use it as presented in the core.<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/223-calboon","name":"Calboon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar223_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"135"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T19:40:37-08:00","id":1282768,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282755#post1282755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how do you deal with a player who likes lunars but is bad at stunting very specific things like attributes? A lot of the players I know only stunt as much as they do because of how easy it is to work in a scene. If I told them they had to stunt in a attribute it would happen a lot less.</div> </div> </div> </div>I feel as though you're approaching the idea in a very narrow manner. I'd be willing to bet that a lot of stunts your players have already come up with would be valid for increasing the dice cap.<br /> <br /> I mean, you talked about the significance of the Excellency in combat, and... is it really so hard to come up with descriptions for attacks that combine Strength with Dexterity?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-25T22:26:16-08:00","id":1282793,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282755#post1282755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">As for the excellency I agree it can be very powerful. I should apologize though my first post on the matter was unclear and I should of waited longer after getting out of bed. My main observation was less that the excellency was objectively weak and more that it could subjectively feel weak to a new player.</div> </div> </div> </div>Ah okay I can understand that.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282755#post1282755\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So how do you deal with a player who likes lunars but is bad at stunting very specific things like attributes? A lot of the players I know only stunt as much as they do because of how easy it is to work in a scene. If I told them they had to stunt in a attribute it would happen a lot less.</div> </div> </div> </div>That could be a problem. As an ST I might loosen up what I'd consider an appropriate stunt for a particular task, if the player is really struggling just include the name of the attribute somehow in the stunt. It's hard to dial in though. If you make it toooo easy than the Lunar excellency is basically the Solar excellency except way better, which isn't really desirable. I think that when the Lunar book drops I might start a thread about helpful stunting and comboing different abilities into those stunts.<br /> <br /> It might not be quite as bad as it seems, honestly for attacks the only one I'm really coming up at a loss for how to easily stunt it in is Stamina. Maybe like, talk about how your character has fought so much in this battle and still shows no sign of tiring at all? But like Charisma, Manipulation, Appearance can all be used to Spiderman/Joker style distract your opponent while you hit them with a sucker punch or just frustrate them, Perception to notice weaknesses, Intelligence for a Robert Downy Jr. style fight analysis, and Wits for super reflexes.<br /> <br /> It's not trivial, that's for sure, and I wouldn't want to try and stunt it for every single attack, but when you really need to cut loose and actually spend a full half of your remaining mote pool into an excellency I think it's doable.<br /> <br /> <br /> It just occurred to me, there's another benefit too, you don't actually have to have any kind of good investment in an attribute to add it, so if you only want a cap of 7-8 you can switch it up to one of your lesser abilities. Being attribute exalted, at least in 2e, not sure about 3e, it was not uncommon for me to see players with like || PHYS:5/5/3 || SOC:3/1/5 || MENT:5/1/5 || as their chargen attribute spreads, and it just goes up from there. After a few dozen xp it would look more like || PHYS:5/5/3 || SOC:3/3/5 || MENT:5/4/5 ||","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T00:26:30-08:00","id":1282805,"title":"","content":"The only actual problem I see is the possibility of your stunts getting stale (which, reminder, is explicitly one of only two circumstances under which you should <i>ever</i> not get at least a one-pointer, the other being droning on for five minutes), but that seems easily fixed by taking advantage of the 95% of actions you aren\u2019t maxing out to mix it up instead of needlessly going for your highest Attribute every time. If that\u2019s really not enough then I\u2019d introduce the idea of a zero-point stunt: The action was boring, but still incorporated an Attribute in a sensible way so you get the dice cap benefit even without getting the +2.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T02:13:13-08:00","id":1282818,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282793#post1282793\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That could be a problem. As an ST I might loosen up what I'd consider an appropriate stunt for a particular task, if the player is really struggling just include the name of the attribute somehow in the stunt. It's hard to dial in though. If you make it toooo easy than the Lunar excellency is basically the Solar excellency except way better, which isn't really desirable. I think that when the Lunar book drops I might start a thread about helpful stunting and comboing different abilities into those stunts.</div> </div> </div> </div>What I hope to see in the book is a good explanation of how often a lunar player is expected to get the increased cap.<br /> It\u2019s possible that mote constraints will end up being the main limiting factor in how often the lunar can really push their cap, in which case the gm can be very generous with awarding the stunts. I can also see the case where the stunt is the limiter (thanks to the discounts from animal shapes) in which case things get more complicated for the gm<br /> <br /> And then there\u2019s the case of spending outside combat when more pools are rarely a problem and the flexibility of the lunar excellency could overshadow other players","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8977-sigfriedmcwild","name":"sigfriedmcwild","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8977_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"50"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T02:43:27-08:00","id":1282819,"title":"","content":"I think it'll get used less out of combat actually, or at least in a less powerful way, because a lot of non-combat rolls are a bit harder to stunt a second attribute into. Not impossible, but harder.<br /> <br /> For example, you generally have to be quite clear if you're using Charisma or Manipulation for a social roll. It's therefore probably a bit difficult to stunt a Charisma roll that's being boosted by Manipulation, but is still a Charisma roll and not a Manipulation roll. Most of the stunts you think of for Charisma are just... Charisma. (Stunting Appearance for Charisma is easier, but maybe your Appearance isn't very good. Certainly one of your social attributes is probably lower than the others).<br /> <br /> Or, let's say you're trying to understand a code. It's Intelligence+Linguistics. Most stunts you think of are just going to be about Intelligence. Stunting that in a way that's about a different attribute rather than just more Intelligence is a bit tricky.<br /> <br /> Or if you're making a Perception+Awareness roll to make out something really far away. The stunts you think of are probably just Perception stunts. Using Wits or Intelligence is pretty tricky. Using Charisma or Appearance or Strength... I can't think of much.<br /> <br /> Whereas, as Isator said, most Dex-based attacks aren't going to be that difficult to stunt with Strength.*<br /> (Although one weird thing is most Lunars are going to be doing lots of stunts on their attacks and defences that are <i>not</i> Dex-based, like &quot;I smash him with a feirce blow&quot; or &quot;I tell him what a great time I had with his dad in the Blue Light district yesterday, then stab him when he's distracted&quot;, but not &quot;I flip right over his sword&quot; or &quot;I move my swords at lightning speed.&quot; Because Dex-based stunts aren't as good as other stunts for attack and Defence.<br /> And of course, the Strength 5 Lunars who've invested in the charm to attack with Strength will do a lot of stunts that don't involve Strength. Probably not Dex either, since their Dex is low, but stunts about their speed and agility are the easiest ones to think of in a fight.)<br /> <br /> Also, I find excellencies get used less out of combat anyway. In social scenes people don't want to throw down 10 motes on an excellency, because pretty quickly you reveal yourself as a horrible Anathema, without the 5m a turn regen. And rolls outside combat are rarely life-and-death.<br /> <br /> Lots of &quot;I spend 4 motes of peripheral&quot; because you don't flare that way. But except for your attributes at 3 (which you may well not have an excellency in anyway), there's no need to get a bigger cap on most rolls.<br /> <br /> <br /> *Though I can see people's ideas getting used up and becoming stale. as Sith_Happens mentioned.<br /> <br /> <br /> Another thing no-one's mentioned is the interaction between animals and dice caps, and how Lunar dice caps change.<br /> My players are not great at dice caps. They get confused by them, especially when we first started playing 3rd ed (despite having played 2nd ed for years).<br /> Now, if they're turning into animals a lot, they're going to need to know their dice-capped rolls. You can't, after all, look at the animal's stats and know your cap.<br /> <br /> I think the best way for this would be for me to make them write down their maxed-out pools for attack and Defence. So say they have Dex 4 and Brawl 3, their capped-out number is 11.<br /> So, when they turn into an animal with 8 dice, they'll be able to buy 3 more, when they turn into an animal with 10 dice, they can buy 1 more, when they turn into an animal with 12 dice they only get to roll 11.<br /> <br /> But the Lunar stunting-excellencies means the cap changes.<br /> So say their cap is 11, and they try and attack with a 13-dice natural attack (Tyrant Lizard claws, etc).<br /> They only get 11. But if they do a +2 dice stunt in a way that's about Strength, they can add, say, 4 more to the cap, giving them a cap of 15.<br /> Now, they've got 15 dice (cap of 13, plus 2 for the stunt) and can buy 2 more.<br /> <br /> That, frankly, will confuse them. They're not idiots, they'll get it, but it'll slow the game down while we work it out. Stunts already do that, but at least they're kind of cool (generally. I got fed up with all the flips. I don't give out stunt bonuses for flips anymore). But this'll make it worse, and slow down combat more.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-26T03:02:13-08:00","id":1282820,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Calboon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1282725#post1282725\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> 1. Never played 1st or 2nd Edition, were lunars fun and interesting in them? If so that makes me feel a lot better about the dice cap, I have only been comparing them to Third edition solars and DB's.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, that's a big question (and the answer is yes, but), but in terms of excellencies specifically;<br /> 2nd ed Lunars could add up to (Attribute) in dice. This was less than, well, anyone else except low-Essence Sidereals. But of course, their excellencies were much more applicable than Solar or DB excellencies, so cost them a lot less (as excellencies weren't free).<br /> <br /> However, they had charms that let you boost the cap for a few rounds/rolls to Attribute+Essence. They all cost a point of willpower.<br /> Relentless Lunar Fury was a Stamina berserker-mode that increased your cap (and made you berserk).<br /> There was also a social one that lasted a few rounds of social combat, and a mental one that lasted much longer but made you mono-focused on that task (so useful for stuff like Crafting artefacts).<br /> <br /> I would say this is probably more powerful than the old ones, but of course Lunar excellencies are no longer cheaper than Solar ones (they're much cheaper than DB ones of course).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> 2. As for overpowered maybe? A lunar needs to spend twice as many attribute dots and twice as many bonus points to match a solar in a single ability and I have no idea if that is fair without seeing the rest of the charms </div> </div> </div>While I agree that, due to restrictions of stunting and cross-applying attributes it's not as powerful as a Solar one, I would hesitate to compare them like that. Yes, it is very difficult to match a Solar in a single ability, but Lunars aren't about Abilities. Their raw max power isn't quite as good, but it's wider.<br /> <br /> In a Lunar's primary attribute set, it's very easy to get 5/5/4 at character gen. You can get 5/5/5 at character gen if you want. And that'll cover all attribute rolls of that type, not just a few abilities.<br /> (Lunars are very good at getting high attributes at character gen generally. What they're rubbish at is abilities. By Essence 3, most well-built Lunars have loads of attributes at 4 and 5, but probably 1 ability at 5 at most. Lots of abilities at 1 or 2 in my experience.<br /> My own essence 5 Lunar, Dr Soma, has attributes of 4/5/5/4/5/3/5/5/5. She only has one ability at 5, one at 4, 5 at 3, and everything else is at 2 or 0.)<br /> <br /> Now, in terms of this excellency, if you're rolling one of your attributes that's 5, and stunting to get another attribute to your cap, there's some chance it's another 5, and a very good chance it's 4.<br /> <br /> I'd say on their primary rolls it's pretty hard for Lunars to get a dice cap of 10 with a stunt, doable to get 9, and easy to get 8.<br /> For secondary or tertiary rolls it's pretty easy with the right stunt to get 6 or 7.<br /> <br /> One interesting thing is that the stunt-cap kind of self-focuses on getting a medium amount. If you have Strength 5, and everything else is less, then on your Strength rolls your cap is going to be 8 or 9. But if you try and seduce someone with your Appearance 3 and your sexy muscles... the cap is still 8, because on your non-Strength rolls you can add 5 to the cap by stunting with Strength.<br /> While I'm not a big fan of this excellency, one thing I do like is that it really helps play a character who's really Strong, or Clever, or Fast, and apply that to everything. If your concept is Snake-totem manipulator who's really good at tricking people, your combat stunts are all about feinting, your intimidation stunts are about looking scarier than you really are, etc (I don't know how you'd apply Manipulation to many mental rolls though).<br /> Or if you're a Monkey-totem genius (called Thoth, presumably), you'll try and come up with combat stunts that are about out-thinking the enemy, manipulation-stunts that are about knowing more than them, etc.<br /> I think it would also work well for certain kinds of Exigents. The Exigent of a god of strength who does Strength-based stunts for everything, for example.<br /> <br /> So that is another way that, while it's difficult for a Lunar to get to 10 with their cap (but not impossible), with stunts your cap is pretty much always going to be decent. Whereas, say, an Eclipse who gets on a boat for the first time in their life, even though being an Eclipse has given them a Sail excellency, might still only have a cap of 3.<br /> <br /> For Solars, it's easier to get the really big numbers on their main rolls, but they're not far ahead. They probably have a bunch of abilities at 5, but only 1 or 2 attributes at 5. So this makes it difficult to get high dice caps on areas they're not really invested in.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 01-26-2019, 07:05 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T19:40:35-08:00","id":1283172,"title":"","content":"This week.... Surely this weeek we will know of the Kickstarter! :maddened gibbering:","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-01-27T22:23:09-08:00","id":1283200,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=