br/>Check out <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1188890-momentum-exalted\" target=\"_blank\">Momentum Exalted!</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6192-simon-darkstep","name":"Simon Darkstep","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"648"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T11:16:02-08:00","id":1284768,"title":"","content":"I just asked Vance elsewhere about the viability of nonbinary or genderfluid Lunars in Exalted third edition, and wanted to cross-post his reply for posterity.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> One of the many things Luna is a goddess of is people who exist outside of gender norms and social conventions<br /> <br /> If you have gender dysphoria, and you Exalt as a Lunar, your true human shape changes into one that you will be comfortable in<br /> <br /> Many-Faced Moon Transformation does let you very easily add, remove, or change sexual characteristics, and its Appearance 1 so everyone can get it, but I didn't want to make trans Lunars have to get that Charm</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-04T11:49:36-08:00","id":1284779,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1284768#post1284768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just asked Vance elsewhere about the viability of nonbinary or genderfluid Lunars in Exalted third edition, and wanted to cross-post his reply for posterity.</div> </div> </div> </div>Vance, thank you. Thank you so much. I am not trans myself, but someone in my close family is, and I've seen them struggle with it for decades.<br /> This small but important details means a ton to me. Thank you from the bottom of my heart.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T19:09:06-08:00","id":1285100,"title":"","content":"Hm, if that happens to a dereth do they drop the gray?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13313-sith_happens","name":"Sith_Happens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13313_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-05T22:37:50-08:00","id":1285126,"title":"","content":"That seems like something for which there are no specific cultural rules, and so it depends on them.<br /> (Even if there are specific cultural rules about if magic changes your genitals, they're a Lunar. They're going to do what they want.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T00:56:13-08:00","id":1285149,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1284768#post1284768\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I just asked Vance elsewhere about the viability of nonbinary or genderfluid Lunars in Exalted third edition, and wanted to cross-post his reply for posterity.<br /> <br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Was this ever in Question? Lunars seemed to always be doing this, and this is Specifically Luna\u2019s schtick. It is interesting to include it in the Basic package when you Exalt, and it\u2019s sensible to have it as Appearance one so everyone can get it.<br /> <br /> But seriously when was this ever I question about it\u2019s Viability? From everything seen with the the Developers and the history of Lunars who would have been surprised about this?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T01:00:23-08:00","id":1285151,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285126#post1285126\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems like something for which there are no specific cultural rules, and so it depends on them.<br /> (Even if there are specific cultural rules about if magic changes your genitals, they're a Lunar. They're going to do what they want.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Solars, Sidereals and Dragon Blooded seem starkly affected by their birth culture and history. And while Lunars are too they seem to have that Tricksy Cultural hero shapeshifter aspect that births new cultures or at least shapes existing ones.<br /> <br /> So basically they don\u2019t have to be defined by their native cultures rules. So basically they would choose if they want to portray as Dereth or not, just like they would choose if they want to live a few Decades as a Giant owl to dream away trauma or if they want to wear the skins if fat Guild Factors or Beautiful Gods.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T01:16:51-08:00","id":1285156,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285149#post1285149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Was this ever in Question? Lunars seemed to always be doing this, and this is Specifically Luna\u2019s schtick. It is interesting to include it in the Basic package when you Exalt, and it\u2019s sensible to have it as Appearance one so everyone can get it.<br /> <br /> But seriously when was this ever I question about it\u2019s Viability? From everything seen with the the Developers and the history of Lunars who would have been surprised about this?</div> </div> </div> </div>Thing is, it's never been made explicit and validated until now, and having the devs come out and say it is important for non-cis fans.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/51-marin","name":"marin","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2019"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T01:37:48-08:00","id":1285157,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>marin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285156#post1285156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Thing is, it's never been made explicit and validated until now, and having the devs come out and say it is important for non-cis fans.</div> </div> </div> </div>Damnit I keep misclicking on my phone tonight! Fourth time! I need to copy and Paste long posts!<br /> <br /> <br /> But it was explicit before this. It was always a Lunar Schtick and a Luna Theme. We even have the Sutra of the Silver Maiden. This was all before 3rd ed, which has for its cover a single Solar in Close up, and it\u2019s a trans male. This is the core book of the Gameline, a trans male getting a solo cover, not a group shot like 2nd ed. And Solars are meant to be the Everyman write large, with heroic proportions. Then we get the Dragonblooded boom and the Immaculate Dragon of Water Mela\u2019s human incarnation is a transgender woman. Arguably the Empresses Most prestigious husband was a transgender man. And we even have an example of a NonBinary Tepet hero.<br /> <br /> Things were explicit before this. It reminds me of a question I asked Vance about if A really worthy mortal was cursed into the shape of a beast like a Falcon when the Exaltations were released how would that work. Vance said they wouldn\u2019t be passed over and the Exaltation of the Sun would likely break the curse or at least return the ability to take the shape of a human again. This is just clarification of how Exaltation works, by giving more in depth rules for Lunars.<br /> <br /> It was always explicit that Lunars often were NonBinary in their outlook and many shifted their genders to the point some couldn\u2019t remember their original forms. This was an accepted and acknowledged thing before we got this Lunar book for 3rd ed. Nothing led me to believe it would be anything but open and accepting to this type of character.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T02:39:54-08:00","id":1285173,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285157#post1285157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> But it was explicit before this. It was always a Lunar Schtick and a Luna Theme. We even have the Sutra of the Silver Maiden. This was all before 3rd ed, which has for its cover a single Solar in Close up, and it\u2019s a trans male. This is the core book of the Gameline, a trans male getting a solo cover, not a group shot like 2nd ed. And Solars are meant to be the Everyman write large, with heroic proportions. Then we get the Dragonblooded boom and the Immaculate Dragon of Water Mela\u2019s human incarnation is a transgender woman. Arguably the Empresses Most prestigious husband was a transgender man. And we even have an example of a NonBinary Tepet hero.<br /> <br /> It was always explicit that Lunars often were NonBinary in their outlook and many shifted their genders to the point some couldn\u2019t remember their original forms. This was an accepted and acknowledged thing before we got this Lunar book for 3rd ed. Nothing led me to believe it would be anything but open and accepting to this type of character.</div> </div> </div> </div>But the fact that it is acknowledged, that people talk about it, that the devs say: this is something we want to include, these are ideas and concepts we want to stand behind, is incredibly important.<br /> Because even if that sidebar hadn't been there, even if Vance hadn't said anything, you could still play a transgender Lunar. But the fact that they say something, the fact they write something and put it in the book and say &quot;this is something we care about&quot; is incredibly important (to me, at least).<br /> I don't think many people in the LGBTQ community want riots and massive changes. They want to be themselves. They want their way of life, their feelings, to be reflected in the books they read and the games they play. I think that is what matters. That they have role models, that they have people they can relate too, even if those are fictional characters.<br /> <br /> <i>I hope I'm not saying anything wrong here. I'm myself not part of the LGBTQ community, but I've known a few people that are, and I've seen some of the things they struggle with. If I said anything wrong, please let me know, but also understand I wasn't trying to offend anyone. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8097-wern212","name":"wern212","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8097_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"377"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T02:51:11-08:00","id":1285175,"title":"","content":"Ugh I need to get a computer my misclicks in my phone tonight are egregious!<br /> <br /> Basically I\u2019m saying your heart is in a good place, you shouldn\u2019t need to tip toe because you aren\u2019t speaking for others only expressing your own personal gratitude. Yes the game is accepting. And it is moving in a positive direction. I have faith in the Dev team.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T03:25:10-08:00","id":1285183,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285157#post1285157\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> the Immaculate Dragon of Water Mela</div> </div> </div> </div>Danaa'd. Mela is Air.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T03:37:59-08:00","id":1285186,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285183#post1285183\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Danaa'd. Mela is Air.</div> </div> </div> </div>I always confuse the two, partly because there was a Selkie Queen Mela in Changeling and that made me think water. ;P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/754-eldagusto","name":"Eldagusto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar754_2.gif","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T04:40:00-08:00","id":1285204,"title":"","content":"I can never spell Sextes Jylis without looking it up. <br /> <br /> Also, &quot;Gee Sextes Jylis, how come Gaia let you have <i>two</i> names?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T05:08:07-08:00","id":1285207,"title":"","content":"I know we've moved on from the Lunar Excellencies but I did get some basic assurances that people wouldn't be incentivised to go &quot;I have Dexterity 5 and Appearance 5 therefore I'm going to stunt all my characters attacks in terms of how sexy they are!&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T05:15:55-08:00","id":1285208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285207#post1285207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know we've moved on from the Lunar Excellencies but I did get some basic assurances that people wouldn't be incentivised to go &quot;I have Dexterity 5 and Appearance 5 therefore I'm going to stunt all my characters attacks in terms of how sexy they are!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Oookay...? I mean, was this a thing that people were really worried about? (And on the other paw, if I want to make a femme fatale type that does fight in this fashion, you are telling me I can't do it?)<br /> <br /> I.e. being able to punch people better with how attractive you are is not a valid playstyle, according to yourself (or your question, or the answer to said question)? Does this also apply to how quickly you think (Int) or how fast you analyze the situation (Wits)?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-06-2019, 08:19 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T05:28:35-08:00","id":1285211,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285207#post1285207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know we've moved on from the Lunar Excellencies but I did get some basic assurances that people wouldn't be incentivised to go &quot;I have Dexterity 5 and Appearance 5 therefore I'm going to stunt all my characters attacks in terms of how sexy they are!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Some attacks <i>should</i> be stunted for how sexy they are, though.<br /> <br /> I think it's important to remember that stunts are only stunts as long as they remain fun. There will be more incentives to stunt as a Lunar, but it's okay for STs to say &quot;no&quot; sometimes too.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T05:33:16-08:00","id":1285214,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ekorren</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285211#post1285211\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Some attacks <i>should</i> be stunted for how sexy they are, though.<br /> <br /> I think it's important to remember that stunts are only stunts as long as they remain fun. There will be more incentives to stunt as a Lunar, but it's okay for STs to say &quot;no&quot; sometimes too.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean, this I agree with, if your stunts are becoming stale, then you don't get anything.<br /> <br /> ...But if you are coming up with interesting descriptions of how your attractiveness blindsides someone, or your strength just breaks through their parry or your almost pre-cognitive intelligence is telling you everything about your quarry down to the resentful slave who did a poor job on buckling his left gauntlet, then let the stunts roll, I say! (In my own capacity as an ST for my games of course, my games might not be similar to your games).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T05:35:39-08:00","id":1285215,"title":"","content":"There's a fine line between effective stunting and Ikki Tousen.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T05:40:18-08:00","id":1285216,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285215#post1285215\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There's a fine line between effective stunting and Ikki Tousen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, but man, let the players and Storyteller decide that. Don't knee jerk put in restrictions on using Appearance in combat to stunt with because you are afraid of a bit of anime smut.<br /> <br /> I get it, we all learnt the lesson from Savant and Sorceror. Sexy not sexist, got it.<br /> <br /> But no one plays Exalted to get stuck with limitations on roleplaying because of prior edition screw ups, y'know.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T06:22:55-08:00","id":1285232,"title":"","content":"From what I've seen of people's issues with the Lunar Excellency, the main concern seems to be that you will be basically forced to always stunt the two highest Attributes you have together. And sure, that would be optimal, but as many have said in this very thread, you don't always need optimal in any given scenario. If you can't creatively add your 5 Strength again to this attack, but had a cool idea to add your 4 Perception, why not take the lower dice cap and probably get a higher stunt rating for the neat idea? The only way I see it becoming a problem is if a character had a rediculously min-maxed Attribute list and only had 2s and 1s in most fields and not stunting in the optimal stat would hardly raise the dice cap at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13696-knurlurzhad","name":"Knurlurzhad","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13696_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"74"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T06:36:22-08:00","id":1285234,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285208#post1285208\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oookay...? I mean, was this a thing that people were really worried about?</div> </div> </div> </div>I know from previous discussions that some of the unease about an excellency contingent on stunting comes from Infernals where having to stunt every action like you were Malfeas etc started really entertaining but ultimately went stale. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">(And on the other paw, if I want to make a femme fatale type that does fight in this fashion, you are telling me I can't do it?)</div> </div> </div> </div>Unless the excellency has changed, you can. <br /> Will there be Appearance charms that allow it to stand in for roles normally assigned to Attributes such as Strength and Stamina? Doubtful.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-06T06:45:01-08:00","id":1285235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Eldagusto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285149#post1285149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Lunars seemed to always be doing this</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't recall off-hand any reference to Lunars having their base human body dramatically transformed to fit their identity before.<br /> <br /> The closest I know of to touching on the subject was Silver Python, and in the time since I've tried to acquaint and concern myself with trans issues, I've found that presentation problematic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T08:37:26-08:00","id":1285576,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285207#post1285207\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know we've moved on from the Lunar Excellencies but I did get some basic assurances that people wouldn't be incentivised to go &quot;I have Dexterity 5 and Appearance 5 therefore I'm going to stunt all my characters attacks in terms of how sexy they are!&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>The reason not to might simply be that you don't generally want to buy 10 dice for every roll though.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knurluzhad</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> From what I've seen of people's issues with the Lunar Excellency, the main concern seems to be that you will be basically forced to always stunt the two highest Attributes you have together.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't my issue with it.<br /> If the player of a character who's main thing is being really, really smart can think of a stunt to explain everything in terms of how she uses her great intelligence for leverage or accuracy or hitting weak spots, then I'm happy for them to do so.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T11:56:17-08:00","id":1285620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285576#post1285576\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The reason not to might simply be that you don't generally want to buy 10 dice for every roll though.<br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>I know this person and what was actually said well enough to reasonably assume I wasn't given a non-answer. Thank you.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:11:39-08:00","id":1285622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285235#post1285235\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I don't recall off-hand any reference to Lunars having their base human body dramatically transformed to fit their identity before.<br /> <br /> The closest I know of to touching on the subject was Silver Python, and in the time since I've tried to acquaint and concern myself with trans issues, I've found that presentation problematic.</div> </div> </div> </div>We haven\u2019t had any official fiction about someone going \u201chuh, I didn\u2019t use to have bunny ears before, and they stick with me through all my forms\u201d in regards to their Tell.<br /> <br /> But we\u2019ve sort of accepted that such a thing happens, and if you can suddenly grow bunny ears upon becoming a Lunar, changing sex doesn\u2019t seem much farther a stretch.<br /> <br /> In one sense it is less of a stretch, since you can learn a Charm to reverse that transformation, but nothing can remove your Tell.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-07-2019, 03:13 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:25:36-08:00","id":1285634,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Knurlurzhad</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285232#post1285232\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">From what I've seen of people's issues with the Lunar Excellency, the main concern seems to be that you will be basically forced to always stunt the two highest Attributes you have together. And sure, that would be optimal, but as many have said in this very thread, you don't always need optimal in any given scenario. If you can't creatively add your 5 Strength again to this attack, but had a cool idea to add your 4 Perception, why not take the lower dice cap and probably get a higher stunt rating for the neat idea? The only way I see it becoming a problem is if a character had a rediculously min-maxed Attribute list and only had 2s and 1s in most fields and not stunting in the optimal stat would hardly raise the dice cap at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>An interesting incentive to have a broader and more versatile set of abilities, sounds Lunar to me.<br /> <br /> Also upon further thought this whole thing might be campaign dependant. If you\u2019re setting it in the Imperial City te fact that you can\u2019t expend 10 motes on an excellency is almost meaningless as you can pretty much do that once (with supplemental charms) before you\u2019re out of personal motes. On the other hand a campaign which is solely about forging out into the Wyld and slaying a panoply of the deadliest Ishvara ever might require more consistently higher caps. That goes double if you\u2019re in a mixed circle with Solars who are always getting theirs.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1121-drlovemonkey","name":"DrLoveMonkey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1121_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4736"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T12:39:20-08:00","id":1285641,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285622#post1285622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We haven\u2019t had any official fiction about someone going \u201chuh, I didn\u2019t use to have bunny ears before, and they stick with me through all my forms\u201d in regards to their Tell.<br /> <br /> But we\u2019ve sort of accepted that such a thing happens, and if you can suddenly grow bunny ears upon becoming a Lunar, changing sex doesn\u2019t seem much farther a stretch.</div> </div> </div> </div>It may not be that much of a stretch to you, but it wasn't something that canonically happened before.<br /> <br /> Having it be something that happens is, well, it's kinda nice.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:13:10-08:00","id":1285658,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285641#post1285641\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It may not be that much of a stretch to you, but it wasn't something that canonically happened before.<br /> <br /> Having it be something that happens is, well, it's kinda nice.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure if you're trying to refute something I said or not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T13:29:57-08:00","id":1285665,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285620#post1285620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know this person and what was actually said well enough to reasonably assume I wasn't given a non-answer. Thank you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">I know from previous discussions that some of the unease about an excellency contingent on stunting comes from Infernals where having to stunt every action like you were Malfeas etc started really entertaining but ultimately went stale.</div> </div> </div> </div>Anyway, this, essentially, is why I dislike it.<br /> <br /> Having played the game for 10 years, our group has found stunting getting a bit stale generally (not completely, but somewhat). For 2 years we've been playing 3rd ed and the Lunar players hardly ever use stunts to get a second attribute.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>DrLoveMonkey</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">An interesting incentive to have a broader and more versatile set of abilities, sounds Lunar to me.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, it may look like it's all about sticking to your Attribute of 5 to every single attribute, but in practice I think you'll want to vary it, and thus have quite a few Attributes at 4.<br /> (I'd say &quot;3 or 4&quot; but what kind of Lunar doesn't have at least 3 in almost everything anyway? My Lunar has Appearance 3 and every other attribute is 4 or 5.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-07T14:34:42-08:00","id":1285692,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1285658#post1285658\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm not sure if you're trying to refute something I said or not.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not particularly; I'm trying to emphasize that, regardless of whether or not you see &quot;you assume the physical characteristics of the gender you identify as when you Exalt as a Lunar&quot; as something that seems fitting for Lunars, the important thing is that the devs made it <i>canon.</i>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T21:42:36-08:00","id":1286092,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1283817#post1283817\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">3 Billion, 392 Million using DD/MM/YYYY compared to just the USA and Phillipines using MMDDYYYY <a href=\"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Date_format_by_country#/media/File:Date_format_by_country_NEW.svg\" target=\"_blank\">https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Date_f...ountry_NEW.svg</a><br /> <br /> I think that shows a right and wrong (USA! USA!)</div> </div> </div> </div>The <b>right </b>way to do it is YYYY/MM/DD. Thus do I say, 2019/02/12. :P","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3487-jetstream","name":"Jetstream","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3487_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"572"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-08T23:32:45-08:00","id":1286102,"title":"","content":"I think we can all agree that both YYYY/MM/DD (biggest to smallest) and DD/MM/YYYY (smallest to biggest) are sensible and logical systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T00:23:24-08:00","id":1286109,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\">DD/MM/YYYY (smallest to biggest)</span></span></span></div></div> </div> </div> </div><div align=\"left\"><span style=\"color:#252C2F\"><span style=\"font-family:Helvetica\"><span style=\"font-size:13px\"><br /> <br /> So when you get past day twelve, you switch them around?<br /> <br /> I would be inclined to put day before month because that's how I'm socialized to use them in speech; the ninth of February feels more natural and logical than February the ninth.</span></span></span></div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T00:26:26-08:00","id":1286111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1286109#post1286109\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So when you get past day twelve, you switch them around?</div> </div> </div> </div>Just out of curiousity, when counting numbers sequentially do you go from, say, 977 to 987?<br /> <br /> prototype00","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T00:31:14-08:00","id":1286114,"title":"","content":"13/02/2019?<br /> I don't see what you're switching? I don't really understand your point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T00:35:03-08:00","id":1286116,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1286114#post1286114\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">13/02/2019?<br /> I don't see what you're switching? I don't really understand your point.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think (but who can fathom the depths of other individuals) that by saying you go from &quot;smallest to biggest&quot;, when the day changes to an integer that is &gt;12 then it will be &quot;bigger&quot; than the month (any month) and will not fit the definition of being &quot;smaller&quot; than the month listed.<br /> <br /> But in doing so, he is ignoring the fact that in the hierarchy of measurements of time, Month is above Day as Hour is above second.<br /> <br /> Or I might be wrong in my assessment, even typing this out it seems a strange conclusion to make.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":8959,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","user":"prototype00","date":". 02-09-2019, 03:38 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T00:48:02-08:00","id":1286119,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>prototype00</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1286116#post1286116\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">who can fathom the depths of other individuals</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, you edited this. Possibly because you found the initial phrasing insulting. I took no offense to it.<br /> <br /> Please, don't equate my irrationalities and overcomplicated speech with depth. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">But in doing so, he is ignoring the fact that in the hierarchy of measurements of time, Month is above Day as Hour is above second.</div> </div> </div> </div>I find this way of describing it slightly circuitous, and loathe how up my alley it ought to make it, but I take the point.<br /> <br /> I would have found short and long to have been clearer than small and large, but that's highly personal and just splitting hairs besides.<br /> <br /> Let's be honest, my initial response was compelled more by the need to act the clever bollocks than anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T00:52:36-08:00","id":1286120,"title":"","content":"Well, my comment was a passive-aggressive joke, so acting the clever bollocks is appropriate.<br /> <br /> (BTW, you've quoted me above but it was actually protoype00 who said it.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T01:15:06-08:00","id":1286121,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1286119#post1286119\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Huh, you edited this. Possibly because you found the initial phrasing insulting. I took no offense to it.<br /> <br /> Please, don't equate my irrationalities and overcomplicated speech with depth. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>In retrospect I do go back and file the rough edges off my replies, to minimize offense where I can.<br /> <br /> As long as nobody has quoted me yet, I don't feel too hung up over it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8959-prototype00","name":"prototype00","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8959_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"964"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T01:19:09-08:00","id":1286123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1286120#post1286120\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">(BTW, you've quoted me above but it was actually protoype00 who said it.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Listen, it's the morning, and I have literally not slept at all, which...<br /> <br /> Never mind that this is a common and basic mistake to make under any circumstances, does not yet seem to be affecting my faculties...<br /> <br /> But I'm sure we can all agree to pretend is for the sake of my pride, right?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T02:42:58-08:00","id":1286129,"title":"","content":"Of course. It's not like it's a mistake I've never made.<br /> <br /> So, how 'bout them Lunars?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 02-09-2019, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T05:16:28-08:00","id":1286148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> how 'bout them Lunars? </div> </div> </div>*vibrates with excitement*","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T05:30:13-08:00","id":1286152,"title":"","content":"Only a few days to go!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T05:59:09-08:00","id":1286156,"title":"","content":"I won't tell anyone what the right way to do calendar dates is, but I can explain the logic behind the American way.<br /> <br /> When you're dealing with a calendar (physical, or electronic), you're usually dealing with the calendar of your current year. The year doesn't matter unless you're going back through old records or projecting forward into future ones. So the year is last.<br /> <br /> After you've opened up the correct calendar, the most important thing to know is which month to look at, since the day won't matter until you do. So the month is the most important number, to confirm if you are already on the right month or if you need to go forward or back.<br /> <br /> That's why the day is considered only the second-most important number, and placed in the middle. Not because of linguistic conventions like &quot;January the 1st&quot; or &quot;4th of July&quot;, but because of the simple logistics of book-keeping.<br /> <br /> .","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>formerly Tornado Wolf, formerly Inugami","edited":{"userid":636,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","user":"Sunder the Gold","date":". 02-09-2019, 09:07 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/636-sunder-the-gold","name":"Sunder the Gold","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar636_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5515"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T07:53:37-08:00","id":1286177,"title":"","content":"I like to add dates to file names when archiving stuff on my computer. It's got to be Year-Month-Day.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://ekorrengames.com\" target=\"_blank\">ekorrengames.com</a><br /> <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/@ekorren\" target=\"_blank\">youtube.com/@ekorren</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/482-ekorren","name":"Ekorren","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar482_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"705"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T08:17:10-08:00","id":1286185,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1286102#post1286102\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think we can all agree that both YYYY/MM/DD (biggest to smallest) and DD/MM/YYYY (smallest to biggest) are sensible and logical systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>DD/MM/YYYYY is only a sensible and logical arrangement of smallest-to-biggest if you write today as 90/20/9102. 09/02/2019 contains no fewer than five instances of bigger-to-smaller ordering (0 tens 9 ones; 0 tens 2 ones; 2 thousands 0 hundreds; 0 hundreds 1 tens; 1 tens 9 ones).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T08:53:42-08:00","id":1286200,"title":"","content":"I mean that years are bigger than months, which are bigger than days. Writing numbers backwards is pedantically confusing.<br /> <br /> All I was trying to say is that both the Arabic-European and East Asian date systems are logical systems.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-09T23:57:02-08:00","id":1286373,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1286200#post1286200\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">All I was trying to say is that both the Arabic-European and East Asian date systems are logical systems.</div> </div> </div> </div>And all I was trying to say was no, the Arabic-European date system is not remotely a logical system.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/572-verzio","name":"Verzio","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar572_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T00:41:14-08:00","id":1286379,"title":"","content":"Because you want to write numbers backwards? That's not how reading works.<br /> <br /> I mean, don't get me wrong. The Chinese system is fine. But so is going day to month to year. Smallest section of time to biggest.<br /> <br /> Why are we even arguing about this?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T03:57:48-08:00","id":1286407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Verzio</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1286373#post1286373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> And all I was trying to say was no, the Arabic-European date system is not remotely a logical system.</div> </div> </div> </div>The numbers aren't relevant. That's just how you write numbers. Ignore them.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-02-10T15:41:32-08:00","id":1286558,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sunder the Gold</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/1272567-lunars?p=1286156#post1286156\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I won't tell anyone what the right way to do calendar dates is, but I can explain the logic behind the American way.<br /> <br /> When you're dealing with a calendar (physical, or electronic), you're usually dealing with the calendar of your current year. The year doesn't matter unless you're going back through old records or projecting forward into future ones. So the year is last.<br /> <br /> After you've opened up the correct calendar, the most important thing to know is which month to look at, since the day won't matter until you do. So the month is the most important number, to confirm if you are already on the right month or if you need to go forward or back.<br /> <br /> That's why the day is considered only the second-most important number, and placed in the middle. Not because of linguistic conventions like &quot;January the 1st&quot; or &quot;4th of July&quot;, but because of the simple logistics of book-keeping.<br /> <br /> .</div> </div> </div> </div>A a Quart is a &quot;Quarter&quot; of a Gallon, but decimal system is still better for anyone after the middle ages. (Ignoring arguments for a base 12 system, which is mathematically better, but the Romans needed their fingers to count to X, so that's too big an ask on changing)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jp